  "reference_notes": "Compared dense leafy scrub, the early spring white flowering thicket and twig/leaf detail to the revised current size pilots 1/4/7 plus all 36 sheet entries. Increased attached terminal fork density from two to four and leaf positions from five to eight while reducing fine twig radius to 4 mm. This gives a denser, irregular thorn-scrub structure without leaf spheres; 25 mm rasterization still exaggerates the thinnest twig widths. Selected late spring leaf flush after the blossom stage, so flowers and autumn sloes are absent. Heights approximately 1.68-3.75 m. Short thorn microdetail cannot be reliably distinguished at this pitch. Accepted as a leafy spring blackthorn thicket source.",
